Article 13

( 1) Children as victims of violence, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 12, also obtain special rights as follows:
a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and/or
e. the right to obtain freedom.
2. In the case of a Child as a perpetrator of sexual violence or a perpetrator of a criminal act, the child has the right to obtain legal assistance and other assistance as well as to obtain special handling related to the confidentiality of their identity.

Article 21

1. Complaint, consultation, and counseling services as referred to in Article 20 letter a shall be carried out by UPTD-PPA to follow up on reports of acts of violence against women and children submitted by victims, families or the community.
2. Services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of: a. interviews and observation of the victim's condition;
b. initial identification or recording of the victim;

12 ­
c. consent for action to be taken;
d. recommendations for follow-up services;
e. coordination and referral to follow-up services and related parties; andf. administration of the complaint process.

Article 28

Forms of empowerment of women victims of violence shall include: a. job training;
b. productive economic enterprises and joint business groups; and c. capital assistance.

Article 23

1. Health services as referred to in Article 20 letter c constitute efforts that include promotive, preventive, curative and rehabilitative aspects for both basic and referral health services.
2. Health services as referred to in paragraph (I) shall include:a. first aid to victims;
b. examination and treatment;
c. follow-up examination of victims;
d. coordination of health rehabilitation implementation;
e. medico-legal examination including collection of evidence from victims and preparation of visum et repertum;
f. supporting and laboratory examination of evidence;
g. consultation with specialist doctors or making referrals; and h. case reporting.

Article 22

Assistance services as referred to in Article 20 paragraph (1) letter b, shall include:
a. accompanying victims during the examination and health recovery process;
b. accompanying victims during the medico-legal process;
c. accompanying victims during the mediation process, examination at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
d. monitoring the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
e. maintaining the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all parties who have no interest, including coverage by the mass media;
f. coordinating with other assistants; and g. providing continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

